  F1_mean_pool_collapses_long: THE lesson's central hypothesis. On SHADE (median 131 steps), MeanPool AUC is materially below both MaxPool and GRU (margin > 0.02 against each). This repo's own cross_trajectory data CONTRADICTS the literature's headline (mean_agg topped that ladder at 0.9358) -- so it is genuinely under test here, not assumed.
  F2_mean_pool_survives_short: On AgentDojo (median 8 steps), MeanPool is NOT materially below MaxPool/GRU (margin <= 0.02 against each). F1 holds AND F2 holds together implicate the HORIZON as the cause; F1 holds AND F2 fails implicates the corpus instead.
